From: hamza <hamza@book4>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom-qmp: suspend USB PHYs during system sleep

- xHCI system suspend: runtime resume of the controller and PHY chain
- PM preparation: extra usage references on providers and generic PHYs
- Runtime-only providers: no clock release after the consumer runtime put
- Observed: four PHYs suspended before entry, all USB3 clocks active at syscore
- Correction: native forced runtime-PM helpers in suspend/resume callbacks
- Existing autonomous wake mode and clock-error handling retained
- Hibernation callbacks and runtime-PM policy unchanged
- Scope: USB and combo drivers used by NP750XQA
- Validation: extracted native PM helpers, both original PM tables rejected
- Hardware suspend, peripheral wake and DisplayPort validation pending
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c | 2 ++
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-usb.c   | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index b94cf2b..6e32d15 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -4115,6 +4115,8 @@ static int __maybe_unused qmp_combo_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops qmp_combo_pm_ops = {
+	.suspend = pm_sleep_ptr(pm_runtime_force_suspend),
+	.resume = pm_sleep_ptr(pm_runtime_force_resume),
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(qmp_combo_runtime_suspend,
 			   qmp_combo_runtime_resume, NULL)
 };
diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-usb.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-usb.c
index d17a89f..fd8db47 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-usb.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-usb.c
@@ -2143,6 +2143,8 @@ static int __maybe_unused qmp_usb_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops qmp_usb_pm_ops = {
+	.suspend = pm_sleep_ptr(pm_runtime_force_suspend),
+	.resume = pm_sleep_ptr(pm_runtime_force_resume),
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(qmp_usb_runtime_suspend,
 			   qmp_usb_runtime_resume, NULL)
 };
